sys_drivers.c: port programs on Windows. Cosmopolitan cannot pass a file
descriptor to another process on Windows, so erl_child_setup cannot work
there. The spawn driver starts each program itself with posix_spawn()
(beam_com_spawn_nt() of c_src/cosmo/beam_com.c), and a thread for each
program gives its exit status to the forker port. The write end of a
port is non-blocking, as on Unix (with the wraps of
c_src/cosmo/beam_com_pipe.c). The driver gives the read end of the
input pipe to beam_com_pipe_reader(), because the free space of the
write end is 0 while the program waits in a large read. os.erl: with
{unix, windows}, find_executable/1 tries the suffixes of Windows (.exe).
See C16 of docs/UPSTREAM.md.

